-# dpl_evolve
-
-`dpl_evolve` is an in-tree sidecar copy of OpenROAD `dpl` for legalizer
-evolution work. It keeps an independent C++ namespace, an independent Tcl
-command set, and a baseline sandbox that compares
-multiple legalizers from the same ORFS handoff point.
-
-## Repo checkout used here
-
-This workspace currently uses:
-
-- ORFS repo: `OpenROAD-flow-scripts` on branch `master`
-- OpenROAD repo: `tools/OpenROAD` checked out as a detached `HEAD`
-
-The detached `HEAD` state in `tools/OpenROAD` is expected here because the
-OpenROAD source is being used as the ORFS submodule checkout rather than as a
-separately managed local branch.
-
-## Repo map
-
-- [`src/`](./src): the independent `dpl_evolve` implementation.
-- [`include/dpl_evolve/`](./include/dpl_evolve): public headers for the sidecar
-  module.
-- [`../../../../evolve_agent/baseline/`](../../../../evolve_agent/baseline/):
-  strict-track, reduced-flow, and DreamPlace baseline harnesses.
-- [`../../../../evolve_agent/knowledge/`](../../../../evolve_agent/knowledge/):
-  planning notes, algorithm cards, and reference material.
-
-## Independent Tcl command set
-
-The baseline `dpl` commands are still available in OpenROAD, but
-`dpl_evolve` also registers a separate Tcl surface so we can experiment without
-changing production command names.
-
-Primary evolve commands live in [`src/Opendp.tcl`](./src/Opendp.tcl):
-
-- `detailed_placement_evolve`
-- `set_placement_padding_evolve`
-- `filler_placement_evolve`
-- `remove_fillers_evolve`
-- `check_placement_evolve`
-- `optimize_mirroring_evolve`
-- `improve_placement_evolve`
-- `detailed_placement_debug_evolve`
-
-The baseline harness can switch between production and evolve commands with
-`--command-set classic|evolve`.
-
