-
-The strict track now runs in two phases:
-
-1. Legalize from `3_4_place_resized.odb` and write `legalized.odb/.def/.sdc`.
-2. Reload `legalized.odb`, run `setRC.tcl`, `check_placement`,
-   `estimate_parasitics -placement`, ORFS `report_metrics`, and a local
-   placement-only metadata normalization step.
-
-That means all baselines now compare post-legalization metrics from the same
-ODB reload path instead of mixing raw legalization output with ad hoc timing
-collection.
-
-The `flow` track is also an explicit reduced Tcl flow now. It does not call
-the full ORFS `detail_place.tcl`; it only runs the placement-stage commands we
-actually want for `dpl_evolve` experiments.
-
-`run_baseline.sh` now drives those Tcl files through tiny generated driver Tcl
-scripts, so the baseline code no longer depends on custom `DPL_EVOLVE_*`
-environment variables.
-
-## How to build
-
-Build the local OpenROAD tree from the ORFS repo root:
-
-```bash
-./build_openroad.sh --local
-```
