-## Which result file to compare
-
-For every baseline run, compare this file first:
-
-`flow/reports/<platform>/<design>/<flow_variant>/dpl_evolve_baseline/<run_tag>/metrics.json`
-
-`metrics.json` is the stable, comparison-friendly summary file. It merges:
-
-- baseline run provenance
-- before/after snapshot displacement
-- HPWL proxy deltas
-- legality status
-- compact legalization summary
-- compact detailed-place stage runtime summary
-- ORFS `report_metrics` output
-- placement-only normalized metadata derived from `3_5_place_dp.json`
-- DreamPlace bridge status when applicable
-
-### Compare these fields first
-
-Across strict and flow baselines, start with:
-
-- `manifest.engine`
-- `manifest.command_set`
-- `manifest.track`
-- `hpwl_proxy.delta_micron`
-- `displacement.average_displacement_micron`
-- `displacement.max_displacement_micron`
-- `timing_metrics.setup_ws`
-- `timing_metrics.setup_tns`
-- `timing_metrics.hold_ws`
-- `timing_metrics.hold_tns`
-- `power_metrics.total`
-- `design_metrics.estimated_wirelength` when present
-- `runtime_seconds`
-
-For legality and run health, also check:
-
-- `legality.placement_violations`
-- `legalization.status`
-
-For DreamPlace runs, also check:
-
-- `dreamplace_bridge.status`
-- `dreamplace_bridge.greedy_legality_check_passed`
-- `dreamplace_bridge.legality_check_passed`
-
-### Supporting JSON files
-
-Inside the same report directory:
-
-- `supporting_files`: relative paths to the raw JSON/TSV files for this run.
-- `run_manifest.json`: run provenance and resolved paths.
-- `legalize_summary.json`: raw legalization-stage summary before ODB reload.
-- `post_metrics_summary.json`: uniform post-legalization ODB reload summary.
-- `metadata.json`: normalized placement-only metadata derived from
-  `3_5_place_dp.json`.
-- `3_5_place_dp.json`: raw ORFS `report_metrics` JSON written during the
-  post-metrics stage.
-- `dreamplace_manifest.json`: DreamPlace bridge status and legality checks.
-- `before_summary.json` / `after_snapshot.json`: flow-track snapshot summaries.
-
-### Practical rule
-
-If you want one file per run, compare `metrics.json`.
-
-If something looks wrong, open the supporting JSON that matches the stage:
-
-- legalization itself: `legalize_summary.json`
-- post-metrics reload/check: `post_metrics_summary.json`
-- ORFS detailed-place metrics extraction: `3_5_place_dp.json` and
-  `metadata.json`
-- DreamPlace bridge: `dreamplace_manifest.json`
