+# dpl_evolve Framework Source
+
+This directory is a prepared OpenROAD sidecar module for the
+`detailed_placement_evolve` command surface.
+
+The prepare patch keeps this source as an evolvable framework with a concrete
+starting pipeline, not a finished legalizer:
+
+- `detailed_placement_evolve` is the evolved command entrypoint.
+- `EvolveLegalizer` owns the top-level hook/telemetry surface.
+- Student algorithms live in private `dpl_evolve` source variants and are
+  built through the lightweight relink path.
+- The default prepared source runs LEGALM-style guidance/legalization and
+  Abacus-enabled negotiation repair when needed. Child agents may aggressively
+  replace or reorder those stages in private variants.
+- Baseline comparison is run by the control repo before Teacher/child
+  optimization begins.
+- Child agents should edit private variant source, relink only `dpl_evolve`,
+  and run strict evaluation with the resulting private OpenROAD binary.
+
+## Interface Contract
+
+The framework boundary is intentionally control-plane only.  `EvolveContext`
+passes small run options such as displacement limits and thread budget; it must
+not become a carrier for per-cell/per-net placement data.  Hot data should stay
+inside the OpenROAD process as node-id keyed contiguous vectors, compact
+row/segment indexes, bounded candidate arrays, and deterministic per-thread
+work buffers.  Avoid JSON, string-keyed maps, cross-process callbacks, or
+`std::function` calls inside inner candidate loops.
+
+Useful implementation references live in the control repo under
+`dpl_evolve_agent/family_variants/`.  The control repo README, AGENTS.md, and
+knowledge files are the canonical human/agent-facing documentation.
